  "summary": "Four August 2026 preprints describe web resources and pangenome graphs that make heterogeneous genomic data queryable and harmonized.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is consolidation of heterogeneous genomic and transcriptomic data into queryable reference-anchored resources. PlantNetX integrates bulk and single-cell RNA-seq for rice, offering Mutual Rank co-expression networks and cell-type expression summaries through a web interface. KlinkPPI queries STRING, BioGRID, IntAct, CORUM, HuRI and Predictomes in one step, mapping identifiers taxonomy-aware. The grapevine collection provides harmonized GATK variant calls for 547 accessions against PN40024v4, and the Pan20 barley pangenome graph, built from MorexV3, supports PAV detection, k-mer imputation, and graph-based mapping. These items differ in organism and data type, so the shared element is integration and access rather than a common inferential method. What is distinctive is explicit attention to identifier handling, cross-dataset harmonization, and reference-anchored variant or sequence representation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
